      "text": "In the late 1990s, maritime interdiction rates for narcotics were below 10 percent due to high-speed smuggling vessels. In response, the U.S. Coast Guard formed an experimental aviation unit, pioneering Airborne Use of Force. The Helicopter Interdiction Tactical Squadron’s success fundamentally changed counter-narcotic strategy.\n\nWe’re proud of HITRON’s 1,000+ drug interdictions. Find out what goes into each one. Monday, we’ll share a deep-dive of this game-changing mission against narco-terrorists.\n\n#USCG #HITRON #MaritimeSecurity #DrugInterdiction\n@DHSgov",
